values
  ('1b504636-f422-5c75-947d-8b6b3195e2c2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The narrator corrects "We did not finish first" with "we did not finish." What does this correction reveal about the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The narrator is confused about the race rules and cannot tell what place the crew earned.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator spins the result hopefully at first, then admits the plain truth in a deadpan way.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator is angry at the officials and wants readers to know the race was unfair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The narrator is boasting that the crew nearly won despite the water in the boat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The narrator spins the result hopefully at first, then admits the plain truth in a deadpan way.$q$, $q$"Did not finish first" implies they finished, and the quick correction exposes that spin with dry honesty. The narrator calls the officials "extremely gracious," so anger does not fit.$q$, 'draft', 'fa642568-bf70-5126-804d-ecbee9e0b069')
