values
  ('dc80f46e-6188-56dd-92b1-b2c33e57ffcd', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The report ends with "Repairs to the hull are underway. Practice resumes Tuesday at dawn." Why might the author have chosen to end with these short, plain sentences rather than a final joke?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The flat ending keeps the deadpan voice and hints at the crew's stubborn, likable determination.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The flat ending shows the narrator has grown ashamed and wants to stop discussing the race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The flat ending reveals that the earlier paragraphs were meant seriously, not humorously.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"},{"text":"The flat ending sets up a sequel in which the crew finally wins a future regatta.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The flat ending keeps the deadpan voice and hints at the crew's stubborn, likable determination.$q$, $q$After a disaster told with understatement, the businesslike close treats the sinking as routine, and returning at dawn suggests persistence. Nothing signals shame, and the tone stays consistent rather than turning serious.$q$, 'draft', 'fa642568-bf70-5126-804d-ecbee9e0b069')
