values
  ('24c464c0-8ebe-501a-9f69-ee11e8fbe9c1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The narrator says the observatories' silence means they "do not want to raise my hopes." What does this reveal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He is losing faith in his discovery and preparing himself for disappointment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"He suspects the observatories have stolen his idea and named the comet themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He understands how observatories work and correctly predicts their response.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"takes-speaker-literally"},{"text":"He interprets every sign in his own favor, which makes him an unreliable narrator.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He interprets every sign in his own favor, which makes him an unreliable narrator.$q$, $q$Silence is a weak sign of interest, yet he reads it as proof of importance, a pattern throughout the journal. He shows no doubt, so losing faith does not fit.$q$, 'draft', '292d4398-3385-5e97-9236-fc0ae5fd6afc')
