  ('0de86ddc-68a4-55c9-a774-bfa8724fbda4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Why might the author have chosen to open with the finished map in the archive rather than with Eliza's work in 1871?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Starting in the present lets the author skip Eliza's story entirely and focus only on the archive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Starting in the present shows that Dr. Mahoe drew the map herself and later forgot about it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Seeing the unfinished line first makes readers wonder why it stops, so the flashback answers a question.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Starting in the present proves the map was printed in the capital as Eliza had been promised.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Seeing the unfinished line first makes readers wonder why it stops, so the flashback answers a question.$q$, $q$The pencil line that "stopped halfway" creates a mystery that the flashback to Eliza resolves. The project was canceled, so the map was never printed.$q$, 'draft', 'a240e601-b238-5151-b51a-ef6370d26827')
