   $q$The second memo "used the word 'efficiency' four times." How does this detail shape the reader's attitude toward the transit office?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the office plans to cancel Route 9, so the driver will soon lose his job.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It mildly mocks the office's rigid focus on rules, setting it against the driver's quiet loyalty.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows the office is unsure what efficiency means, so the memo is full of mistakes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows the office is right, so readers should side with it against the stubborn driver.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It mildly mocks the office's rigid focus on rules, setting it against the driver's quiet loyalty.$q$, $q$Counting the repeated word makes the memo sound mechanical and insistent, which contrasts with the human reason for the stop. Nothing in the text mentions canceling the route.$q$, 'draft', 'a9123e74-bca1-54be-abb7-f001a6a34f4f')
